'''''Dischidia formosana''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Apocynaceae]].<ref name=COL>{{Catalogue of Life |id=6CZ5D |title=''Dischidia formosana'' Maxim. |access-date=February 26, 2026}}</ref> It is native to [[Taiwan]] and the Japanese chain of [[Ryukyu Islands]] that stretch southwest from [[Kyushu]] to Taiwan.<ref>{{cite POWO |id=96939-1 |title=Dischidia formosana }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |last1=Eggli |first1=Urs |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=gf3uCAAAQBAJ |title=Etymological Dictionary of Succulent Plant Names |last2=Newton |first2=Leonard E. |date=2013-06-29 |publisher=Springer Science & Business Media |isbn=978-3-662-07125-0 |pages=86 |language=en}}</ref> Like other ''Dischidia'' it has a climbing growth habit, producing smooth, round leaves and tiny white flowers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Dischidia formosana in Flora of China @ efloras.org |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=200018597 |access-date=2022-10-16 |website=www.efloras.org}}</ref> Though not particularly rare in Taiwan, the species is on the [[Japanese Red List]] as a critically endangered plant.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Global Red List of Japanese Threatened Plants >> Specimens & Database :: National Museum of Nature and Science, Tokyo |url=https://www.kahaku.go.jp/english/research/db/botany/redlist/list/list_04_052_1.html |access-date=2022-10-16 |website=www.kahaku.go.jp}}</ref>

